#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1085 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "Pins the NEW inner-join semantics: subject 004 has LBDY populated and a COMPLETE LBDTC, but no DM record at all. Under the removed Join_Type: left, DM.RFSTDTC was null after the merge, read as 'not a complete date', and this rule fired claiming an imputed day value; the inner join drops the row instead -- D-TA-2 (inner is the doctrine): a subject absent from DM is PMDA-SD0064's finding, not this rule's -- one root cause, one finding. DM is present and non-empty (subject 001, RFSTDTC complete), so a rule that still left-joined WOULD fire here: this is a discriminator, not a vacuous pass."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
col LBDY  type=Num  label="Study Day of Specimen Collection"
---
S1 | LB | 004 | 1 | ALB | 2023-06-25 | 5
---

dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFSTDTC type=Char label="Subject Reference Start Date/Time"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2023-06-01
